From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] video: meson: add MIPI DSI output

The VPU driver knew CVBS and HDMI. Add the third output of the G12A,
G12B and SM1: the ENCL encoder feeding the Synopsys DesignWare MIPI DSI
host, as in Linux (meson_encoder_dsi.c, meson_dw_mipi_dsi.c, the ENCL
parts of meson_venc.c).

meson_dw_mipi_dsi: a video bridge for "amlogic,meson-g12a-dw-mipi-dsi",
with the generic dw_mipi_dsi host and the AXG/G12A D-PHY. The U-Boot
G12A clock driver has neither the GP0 PLL nor the video clocks, so it
sets them itself: GP0 at the lane bit rate, the D-PHY bit clock GP0/1,
the pixel clock GP0 / (bpp / lanes) through VCLK2 to CTS_ENCL.

The order is that of Linux: host and D-PHY up in command mode and the
panel init commands, then the encoder, then video mode and the
backlight. Fed pixels while still in command mode, the host overflows
its DPI FIFO and never puts the data lanes in HS: black screen.

The VPU takes this path when the DSI node on its DPI port (port 2) is
enabled. The panel node's "rotation" turns the console. The OSD stays
in RGB: neither the OSD1 RGB->YUV matrix nor the POST2 matrix.
---
